title: Vertical Network Scan
id: bd623729-bd3e-4900-9e25-17b2657b500e
status: experimental
description: Detects a vertical network scan. This is the type of scan that occurs when looking for several different destination ports on a single destination IP. The objective of this type of scan is to examine all services available on a device. 
references:
    - https://attack.mitre.org/techniques/T1046/
tags:
    - attack.discovery  
    - attack.t1046      
author: ferezito  
date: 2025/04/14 
logsource:                      
    category: firewall  
detection:
    selection:
        Log_Type: Traffic
        Protocol: 
            - TCP
            - UDP
    aggregation:
        DstPorts|gt: 49
        Timeframe: 5m   
    condition: (selection and aggregation) by SrcIp
fields:
    - SrcIP
    - DstIP
    - DstPort
    - Action
falsepositives:
    - Authorised vulnerability scanners
    - Network monitoring tools
level: low
